---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets'
import Landscape from '@assets/landscape.jpeg'
---

<section class="mx-auto mt-8 w-[90%] sm:mt-12 2xl:w-[60%]">
  <h2
    class="mb-3 scroll-m-20 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight transition-colors"
  >
    🗃️ About me?
  </h2>
  <p class="text-sm sm:text-lg md:text-xl">
    I started programming in 2018 with <strong>PHP</strong> and <strong
      >C++</strong
    > through school programs. I switched to <strong>JavaScript</strong> to pursue
    web development. I touched <strong>Java</strong> and <strong>C#</strong> because
    of college (against my will).<br /><br />
    But in the last few years, I've been enjoying using <strong>C</strong>, <strong
      >Go</strong
    >, and <strong>Rust</strong>.
    <br /><br />
    I feel comfortable designing and implementing product-oriented software: scripting,
    automation, CLI development, database repositories, REST APIs, and services.
  </p>

  <div class="mt-10">
    <Image
      src={Landscape}
      alt="Landscape"
      class="mx-auto rounded-sm border"
      width={360}
    />
    <p class="mt-3 w-full text-center text-xs opacity-80 sm:text-sm">
      Mandatory scenery picture. Otherwise this page becomes a wall of text.
    </p>
  </div>

  <details open class="mt-8" name="info">
    <summary> Programming Languages </summary>
    <p>
      I have touched a (IMO) fair number of programming languages (I didn't list
      all of them). I don't have a favorite; most of the time, I use whichever
      one I consider the best fit for the task at hand. But I enjoy using all of
      them in their own way.<br /><br />
      I enjoy understanding their ergonomics and the reasons behind their design decisions.
    </p>
  </details>

  <details class="mt-4" name="info">
    <summary> Frameworks </summary>
    <p>
      Over time, I've also touched a few different frameworks. I frequently use <strong
        >Next.js</strong
      >, <strong>SvelteKit</strong>, and <strong>Astro</strong> for web development.<br
      /><br />
      <strong>Express</strong> and <strong>Fastify</strong> were common tools that
      I used for a long time. More recently, I've been preferring <strong
        >Fiber</strong
      > (fasthttp), because of Go.
    </p>
  </details>

  <details class="mt-4" name="info">
    <summary> Service Development </summary>
    <p>
      In general, I've been working with REST APIs: from SQL query design and
      third-party library integration to communication between services,
      authentication flow design, and endpoint handler implementation.
      <br /><br />
      I'm familiar with <strong>Docker</strong>, <strong>Linux</strong>, most
      package managers, <strong>Git</strong>, and cloud providers.
    </p>
  </details>
</section>
